## Method (be systematic — the app is large)

1. Inventory the OLD app first. Enumerate every data operation, endpoint, action, filter, RLS policy, SQL function, and auth flow. Cite file paths and line numbers as evidence.
2. Then inventory the NEW Django app the same way.
3. Match them up. For each OLD capability, find its NEW counterpart or mark it missing.
4. **Do not guess or assume.** If you haven't read the file, say so. Every "present"/"missing" verdict must point to actual code (file path + line). If something is ambiguous, list it under "Needs human verification" rather than guessing.
5. Work in passes if the codebase is too big for one go: do it module by module (e.g. one resource/domain at a time — users, orders, products...) and keep appending to the report.

